NXR-171|Optional lifecycle compatibility|Kernel lifecycle|A future lifecycle profile shall use boot-reserved thread slots while preserving sealed registration and permanent completion in the default profile.|Runtime lifetime support need not imply dynamic allocation but must not silently alter the current contract.|Default post-start create still fails; lifecycle-disabled binaries expose no runtime recycling path.|Compile both profiles and execute default registration regressions plus opt-in slot state fixtures.|NXR-001,NXR-128,NXR-129|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Fixed slot and stack pool; zero general heap; lifecycle remains opt-in.|include/rtos.hpp,src/kernel.cpp,include/rtos_mutex.hpp,include/rtos_queue.hpp|Runtime lifetime support need not imply dynamic allocation but must not silently alter the current contract.
